# Cloudflare Pages redirects for turonsf.com
#
# v3 endorsement hub: the campaign pages were retired and every legacy route
# lands on the same-language hub with a 301, so search engines pass the old
# pages' links to the hub. v2 is preserved at tag v2-campaign-site-final;
# restoring it means removing these rules, and browsers that cached a 301 may
# keep redirecting until their cache clears.
#
# Keep this file SHORT. In production this project applied only the first 101
# rules of a 174-rule file (2026-10-15), well under Cloudflare's documented
# 2,000 static / 100 dynamic limits. So each retired page is one splat per
# language: "/es/about*" covers /es/about, /es/about/ and anything below it
# ("/thank-you*" also covers /thank-you-volunteer). Never splat "/en": it would
# swallow /en/sitemap.xml. bin/check-redirects.sh enforces this in CI.
#
# www -> apex is a Cloudflare zone redirect rule, not something this file does.

# Aliases from v2
/give*                    /                 301
/uesf-questionnaire*      /                 301
/en                       /                 301
/en/                      /                 301

# llms.{lang}.txt (v2 naming) -> Hugo-rendered llms.txt per language
/llms.en.txt              /llms.txt         301
/llms.es.txt              /es/llms.txt      301
/llms.yue-Hant.txt        /yue-hant/llms.txt 301
/llms.zh-Hant.txt         /zh-hant/llms.txt 301
/llms.zh-Hans.txt         /zh-hans/llms.txt 301
/llms.tl.txt              /tl/llms.txt      301
/llms.vi.txt              /vi/llms.txt      301
/llms.ar.txt              /ar/llms.txt      301


